      "longitude": "Native conventions differ: CMIP6 and ERSSTv5 are 0-360, WOA23 and SEANOE -180-180, GLODAP 20.5-379.5. Nothing converts them; bring products to one convention before comparing or sub-setting across them.",
      "depth": "CESM2's lev is in centimetres (its lev_bnds declare metres), the rest in metres; all positive down. Nothing converts them.",
      "grid": "CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are curvilinear and cannot be sel'd by lat/lon directly; use a 2-D mask. Area weighting of model fields uses the model's areacello.",
      "time": "WOA23 needs decode_times=False; SEANOE's time carries no CF units; CMIP6 uses three different calendars (CESM2 noleap / 365_day, GFDL-ESM4 noleap, MPI-ESM1-2-LR proleptic_gregorian), so their time axes decode to different types and must be aligned before they are combined.",
      "units": "CMIP6 uses mol m-3 (per volume), WOA23 and GLODAP use umol kg-1 (per mass); converting between them needs in situ density, mol m-3 = umol kg-1 * rho / 1000. Nothing converts them.",
      "climatology_period": "WOA23 temperature/salinity 1971-2000 or 1991-2020, oxygen/AOU/percent-saturation 1971-2000 or 1965-2022, nutrients (nitrate/phosphate/silicate) 1965-2022 ONLY; GLODAP 1972-2013; ERSSTv5 internal climatology 1971-2000; CPC uses 1991-2020 from 2021-01 onward."
